      "math_academy_id": "q-225063",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5)$ given below, compute $P(2<X<4).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0067\\,$ | $\\,0.0404\\,$ | $\\,0.1247\\,$ | $\\,0.2650\\,$ | $\\,0.4405\\,$ | $\\,0.6160\\,$ | $\\,0.7622\\,$ |\n\n$P(2<X<4)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(X<4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X<4) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X<4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<4) & =F(3)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.2650-0.1247 \\\\  & =0.1403.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
